  <PageHeader
    eyebrow="SDAHC Research"
    title="Australian SDA Statistics"
  />
  <section class="section"><div class="prose">
    <p>Australia had 13,779 enrolled Specialist Disability Accommodation dwellings as at 31 March 2026 (NDIA, Q3 2025-26; analysis: SDAHC Research). This page is maintained by SDAHC Research as a reference source for SDA market figures, with every number dated and defined. It is updated each quarter as new NDIA data is released.</p>

    <h2>Key SDA figures at a glance</h2>
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Measure</th><th>Figure</th><th>As at</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Enrolled SDA dwellings (national)</td><td>13,779</td><td>31 March 2026</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Growth since Q4 2022-23</td><td>+74%</td><td>Q3 2025-26</td></tr>
        <tr><td>New dwellings enrolled per week</td><td>13</td><td>Q3 2025-26</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Participants living in SDA</td><td>16,263</td><td>Q3 2025-26</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Participants with SDA funding</td><td>25,633</td><td>Q3 2025-26</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Participants not utilising SDA funding</td><td>9,370</td><td>Q3 2025-26</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Active SDA providers</td><td>563</td><td>Q1 2025-26</td></tr>
        <tr><td>High Physical Support share of supply</td><td>49%</td><td>Q3 2025-26</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Annualised SDA funding in participant plans</td><td>~$653 million</td><td>Q3 2025-26</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <h2>Dwellings, places and participants are not the same thing</h2>
    <p>Published SDA figures are frequently inconsistent because three distinct measures are reported interchangeably. Comparing a dwelling count against a place count, or a funded participant against a resident participant, produces figures that appear to contradict each other when they are simply measuring different things.</p>
    <p>The gap between the last two matters commercially. As at Q3 2025-26, 25,633 participants held SDA funding but only 16,263 were living in SDA, leaving 9,370 participants with approved funding they were not using. From Q4 2024-25 the NDIA began reporting this cohort separately as "eligible, not yet using SDA", which means participant figures before and after that change are not directly comparable.</p>
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Term</th><th>What it counts</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Enrolled dwelling</td><td>A physical property enrolled with the NDIA as Specialist Disability Accommodation. One dwelling typically contains more than one resident place.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Resident place</td><td>An individual participant position within an enrolled dwelling. Place counts are therefore higher than dwelling counts.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Participant with SDA funding</td><td>A person whose NDIS plan includes approved SDA funding. Approval does not mean the person is currently living in an SDA dwelling.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Participant living in SDA</td><td>A person actually residing in an enrolled SDA dwelling.</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>

