    <h2>How these figures are sourced and updated</h2>
    <p>All dwelling, participant and funding figures on this page are drawn from NDIS Supplement P, Specialist Disability Accommodation, the NDIA's quarterly public dataset. The most recent period used is Q3 2025-26, with data as at 31 March 2026. Historical comparisons use Q4 2022-23 as the baseline, being the earliest period with consistent Supplement P coverage for these measures.</p>
    <p>This page is reviewed and updated by SDAHC Research each quarter as the NDIA publishes new data. Figures are reproduced for analytical purposes; readers should refer to original NDIA publications for definitive figures. Full source list and methodology are documented on our <a href="/research/research-methodology/">methodology page</a>.</p>

    <h2>Citing these figures</h2>
    <blockquote>SDAHC Research, &ldquo;Australian SDA Statistics&rdquo;, SDA Home Choices, Brisbane, 2026.</blockquote>
    <p>Individual figures and brief quotations may be reproduced with attribution to SDAHC Research. Commercial interpretation of these figures, including observed transaction yields, the gap between enrolled and actual income, and sale prices relative to enrolled value, is published in the SDA Market Report 2026.</p>
    <p><a class="btn b1" href="/research/sda-market-report-2026/">Get the SDA Market Report 2026</a></p>
